UPSTREAM.json lists each source file, its SHA-256 digest, and local adaptations.

AReaL adaptations require a Main-owned target Session and a temporary
WebContents registration callback. They remove ZCode partition selection,
legacy profile-path compatibility, data-clearing ownership, and site-permission
dependencies. Local types replace @zcode/shared. SQLite loads lazily and reports
an explicit unavailable result. Windows App-Bound decryption is unsupported
because AReaL does not ship ZCode's signed Windows helper. The public product
entry supports macOS only. Portable upstream discovery and decryption sources
remain available internally. Temporary Electron windows are destroyed and
unregistered after initialization and registration failures.

The package includes AReaL build scripts and synthetic acceptance fixtures.
